{number: 91}
{title: Jesus, Lover of My Soul}
{key: F}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[F] Jesus, Lover [Bb] of my [F] soul,
Let me to Thy [C7] bosom [F] fly,
While the nearer [Bb] waters [F] roll,
While the tempest [C7] still is [F] high:
Hide me, O my [Bb] Savior, [F] hide,
Till the storm of [C7] life is [F] past;
Safe into the [Bb] haven [F] guide;
O re-[C7] ceive my soul at [F] last.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[F] Other refuge [Bb] have I [F] none;
Hangs my helpless [C7] soul on [F] Thee;
Leave, ah! leave me [Bb] not a-[F] lone,
Still support and [C7] comfort [F] me.
All my trust on [Bb] Thee is [F] stayed,
All my help from [C7] Thee I [F] bring;
Cover my de-[Bb] fenseless [F] head
With the [C7] shadow of Thy [F] wing.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[F] Plenteous grace with [Bb] Thee is [F] found,
Grace to cover [C7] all my [F] sin;
Let the healing [Bb] streams a-[F] bound;
Make and keep me [C7] pure with-[F] in.
Thou of life the [Bb] Fountain [F] art,
Freely let me [C7] take of [F] Thee;
Spring Thou up with-[Bb] in my [F] heart;
Rise to [C7] all eterni-[F] ty.
{end_of_verse}
